~ go_left
Path narrows. Ferns whisper across your knees.
do AudioManager.current_speaker = AudioManager.narrator
NARRATOR: Left is the traditional direction for mistakes.
do AudioManager.current_speaker = null
A small lantern glow winks ahead, then dips out of sight.
=> gate_to_clearing

~ go_right
Needles scuff. An old sign points at nothing in particular.
do AudioManager.current_speaker = AudioManager.narrator
NARRATOR: Right feels right, until it doesn’t.
do AudioManager.current_speaker = null
do AudioManager.rope_creak.play()
You hear rope creak. (Or wind. You decide it’s wind.)
=> gate_to_clearing

~ go_back
You turn around. The trail behind now looks slightly rearranged.
do AudioManager.current_speaker = AudioManager.narrator
NARRATOR: Back is wonderful… when permitted.
do AudioManager.current_speaker = null
Your next step sets you down forward anyway. 
=> gate_to_clearing

~ stand_still_1
Time puts a hand on your shoulder and doesn’t squeeze.
do AudioManager.current_speaker = AudioManager.narrator
NARRATOR: I love stillness. The forest does, too. It keeps you.
do AudioManager.current_speaker = null
A firefly floats ahead, patient. The path brightens a notch.
=> line_3

~ stand_still_2
do AudioManager.current_speaker = AudioManager.narrator
NARRATOR: I love stillness. The forest does, too. It keeps you.
do AudioManager.current_speaker = null
=> line_4

~ follow_firefly
It blinks like a metronome for your feet.
do AudioManager.current_speaker = AudioManager.narrator
NARRATOR: Following tiny lights is how we decorate bad ideas.
do AudioManager.current_speaker = null
=> gate_to_clearing

~ loop_thrice
do AudioManager.current_speaker = AudioManager.narrator
NARRATOR: You’re hoping the forest will invent a door. It will. I’ve seen the draft.
do AudioManager.current_speaker = null
=> gate_to_clearing

~ gate_to_clearing
The trees lean away at the same time, as if hushed by a teacher.
do get_parent().transition_animations.play_fade_out()
[next=2]
do AudioManager.current_speaker = AudioManager.narrator
NARRATOR: Ah. Here we are. The part with the hole.
do AudioManager.current_speaker = null
=> END!